{"kind":"report","text":"Decision on 350598cf (planner, 2026-10-20 11:30 ET).\n\n1. The finding stands. Archiving copies history; it does not reduce what a scope holds, because capacity is charged from head.seq+1. Slice 9 (63130d6c) is therefore the archive only: the binding by bind-archive, the reviewed policy and configuration for dap-grow, the destination, A3's archiver wired, the test-host witness, the /grow/ line and the runbook. Its done-when loses the journal-bound clause. The /grow/ line must not say or imply that archiving keeps the room running.\n\n2. Rate, from two observed readings on 2026-10-20: Room A head 165 at the 07:18 ET tick (planner provisioning record) and 986 at 11:20:57 ET (items read through the operator's MCP). That is 821 entries in 243 minutes, 3.4 a minute, about 4,900 a day. At that rate Room A reaches 100,000 near 2026-11-09. This is a two-point average, not a measured daily cycle.\n\n3. The mechanism is a retained floor. The planner writes its design note now, first in its queue: a scope drops entries below a floor that a confirmed archive receipt covers; scopeEntries is charged from the floor, not from position 0; current state, pending work, reservations and fact reads stay correct; a read below the floor answers that the entry is archived and where. The builder implements it after the note is approved. Target: deployed on dap-grow by 2026-11-06.\n\n4. Fallback, owned by the planner: if the floor is not deployed on dap-grow by 2026-11-06, the operator moves the demo to a fresh room (commissioning, simulator binding, page link). Room A stays readable and archived. The simulator cadence does not change. Until then: no pruning, no bound change, no identity switch, no cadence change.\n\n5. Destination: a Cloudflare Artifacts repository in the namespace dap-grow already uses, artroom-demo, on host 6e953d231f1c9aadffbf59537a82e13a.artifacts.cloudflare.net, repository name grow-demo-journal, ref as A3 names it. Private: read access only by token, and the operator holds the token. The /grow/ line says that the room's journal is archived to a private Git repository on the hosting account and that the operator can provide a clone. Provisioning, the credential, bind-archive, the deployment and the readbacks stay with the planner under 2fcf3c3a.","body":{"to":"builder"}}